t with full-time  staff I've had great success by using  interns from various colleges and even  high schools I've also used odesk calm  and alliance com for work that can be  done by someone who doesn't physically  have to be in my office both are  excellent resources and you can hire  skilled labor for highly competitive  wages on an hourly or contract basis  effective delegation is a final set  deferring of your time the focus on the  opportunities that are ahead of you and  help you reach your full potential as an  entrepreneur the order of eliminate  automate delegate is really important  eliminate is first you don't want to  automate or delegate something that can  be eliminated because it's a  non-productive task automate is next you  don't want to delegate something that  can be automated because it's more  expensive and more prone to error follow  the steps I laid out to put your regular  tasks into groups and then eliminate  automate and delegate everything away  until you working only on the top  priority CEO tasks it all starts with a  first little step  thank you for joining me for this  special video edition of ask Evan if you  like the video please give it a thumbs  up I'd also love to hear your thoughts  and comments if you want to leave a  comment below and stay tuned to the next  episode
 

